.TH CORE 5 "March 2026" "Substrate" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
core \- Substrate kernel core-dump policy record
.SH DESCRIPTION
Substrate currently exposes core-dump handling as a kernel policy hook rather
than a persistent on-disk core-file writer.
.PP
When a process terminates due to a signal whose default action includes
.BR SA_CORE ,
the kernel calls
.BR coredump ()
before exit if
.BR RLIMIT_CORE
permits it.
.PP
The current in-kernel core record captures:
.IP \(bu 2
process identity metadata
.IP \(bu
signal number, trap code, and trap address
.IP \(bu
saved user register state when the fatal path supplies a trap frame
.IP \(bu
personality-specific segment metadata where available
.PP
For
.B ELKS
processes, the captured record includes the visible 16-bit register image and
the active private-LDT descriptor set used for
.BR CS ,
.BR DS ,
.BR SS ,
and related selectors.
.PP
Substrate does not yet emit a persistent ELF core file. The current contract is
that the kernel captures a stable crash record and sets the
.B WCOREDUMP
wait-status bit when the hook succeeds.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR signal (2),
.BR wait (2),
.BR personality_elks (7)
